            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0580" n="504" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.001G291/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-06T17:00:00-05:00">November 6, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. The Department is today acknowledging without comment the receipt of the
                    following communication from the Greek Minister dated November 5: <pb
                        facs="0581" n="505" xml:id="pg505"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“By direction of the Royal Government of Greece, I have the honor to
                            bring to your knowledge that, following the confirmation of the
                            resolution of the National Assembly given by the Greek people through
                            their plebiscite of last Sunday, regarding the restoration of the
                            Constitutional Monarchy, His Majesty King George II will return to
                            Greece shortly to assume his royal duties.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>As soon as the Department is officially notified that the King has assumed his
                    duties new letters of credence will be sent to you for presentation if and when
                    similar action is taken by your British and French colleagues.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
